    <h1 class="doc-title">TEST DESIGN SPECIFICATION (TDS) - PRE-LAB</h1>

    <h2 class="section-title">1. Requirements</h2>
    <p><strong>RQ-001:</strong> The system shall allow students to register for an available course.</p>
    <p><strong>RQ-002:</strong> The system shall prevent students from registering for a course that has reached maximum capacity.</p>
    <p><strong>RQ-003:</strong> The system shall prevent students from registering for the same course twice.</p>
    <p><strong>RQ-004:</strong> The system shall allow students to view the list of courses they have successfully registered for.</p>
    <p><strong>RQ-005:</strong> The system shall display an appropriate message indicating that no registration records are available when no courses have been registered.</p>

    <h2 class="section-title">2. Feature Sets</h2>

    <div class="fs-block">
        <div class="fs-title">FS-001 – Course Registration</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Objective: Manage student course enrollment and enforce capacity and duplicate constraints.</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Priority: High</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Traceability: RQ-001, RQ-002, RQ-003</div>
    </div>

    <div class="fs-block">
        <div class="fs-title">FS-002 – Registered Courses Management</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Objective: Display enrolled courses and handle empty registration history.</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Priority: Medium</div>
        <div class="fs-detail">Traceability: RQ-004, RQ-005</div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title">3. Test Conditions</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th width="14%">ID</th>
